# One person, one name, however many addresses they have committed under.
#
# `git shortlog -sn` and `git log %aN/%aE` read this, and so does
# scripts/release-notes.sh -- which decides whose name to put against a line by
# comparing addresses, and would otherwise credit the maintainer as a
# contributor to their own release for the commits made from a second machine.
#
# Add a line when somebody turns up twice. Nothing else needs it.

